summary:
- topic: Board and Student Representative Updates
  text: The board acknowledged new student representatives and announced Superintendent
    Angela Atkinson Duina's upcoming resignation, initiating a transition plan. Student
    reports highlighted successful high school graduation, summer credit recovery,
    mental health advocacy, and various end-of-year activities across all school levels.
- topic: District Progress and Achievements
  text: Superintendent Angela Atkinson Duina reported significant improvements in
    student attendance, a reduction in chronic absenteeism, enhanced school culture
    through PBIS, and a notable increase in SAT scores and elementary student growth
    goals.
- topic: School Safety and Facilities Upgrades
  text: Updates on school facilities included the planned installation of security
    cameras and secure vestibules at elementary schools, with three schools slated
    for completion this summer. The Director of Operations and Safety confirmed bids
    came in under budget, accelerating the timeline for some projects.
- topic: Community Partnerships and Career Exploration
  text: The Community Partnerships report showcased extensive volunteer engagement,
    food security initiatives, career exploration programs (ELOs), and various community
    donations supporting students and schools. Board members and student representatives
    praised the ELO program's impact.
- topic: Grant Funding and Pre-K Partnerships
  text: The Assistant Superintendent announced the award of a second Community School
    Grant and a new Climate Education Grant. An update on Pre-K partnerships confirmed
    12 funded seats with Chickadee, with a United Way partnership anticipated for
    Fall 2026.
- topic: ESEA Federal Funding Changes
  text: The ESEA funding report detailed decreases in Title I and Title IV allocations,
    with Title II and III funding still unknown. This prompts a cautious outlook for
    future budget planning, though current year positions are not impacted.
- topic: Staff Recognition and Retirements
  text: The board recognized Monica Malcomson as the 2025 Cumberland County Teacher
    of the Year and honored nine long-serving retirees for their collective 242 years
    of dedication to the district.
- topic: Board Communications and Budget Referendum
  text: Board members reiterated their strong commitment to student mental health
    and wellbeing, praised the recent joyful graduation ceremony, and urged community
    participation in the upcoming school budget referendum vote.
